{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"boredom in games boredom in games","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","fileName":"Boredom in Games.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Boredom in Games","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Challenge Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Challenge Design","Game Difficulty","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"boredom in games boredom in games","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","fileName":"Boredom in Games.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Boredom in Games","heading":"Boredom in Games","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Boredom in games can occur when the player's mastery exceeds the demands of the activity and the system asks only for repetition of already understood actions. Resistance remains, but it no longer produces significant learning or choice.\n\nAvoiding boredom does not require constant escalation. New relationships, altered pacing, wider choices, or a deliberate reflective pause can change the experience without simply increasing [[Game Difficulty|difficulty]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Challenge Design","Game Difficulty","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"boredom in games boredom in games","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Boredom in Games.md","fileName":"Boredom in Games